    "top_frame": "Randy V\u00e1squez pitched a shutout and the Padres never trailed.",
    "what_this_means": "This is a team learning to win on margins. V\u00e1squez held Seattle scoreless over six innings. Four hits, three strikeouts, complete control. And the bullpen did not blink. Morejon, Adam, and Miller combined for three scoreless innings, with Miller recording four strikeouts in 1.1 frames to close it out. The offense left nine runners on base across the game, converting just one RISP situation into a run, yet still finished the night with 2\u20130. That is not carelessness. That is efficiency disguised as restraint. They got what they needed in the fourth inning and held it. In a division where every game moves the margin, holding a one-run lead into the ninth is becoming their calling card. And it is working.",
